@startuml sequence_diagram_login_role_resolution
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - AA03 Role Resolution after Login (local login + loading the current roles in the SPA)

actor User as "Client / User"
participant SPA as "SPA (Front-End)\nAuthProvider / authApi"
participant Routes as "AuthRoutes"
participant Controller as "AuthController"
participant AuthMW as "AuthMiddleware"
participant Service as "UserService"
participant Repo as "IUserRepository"
database DB as "Database\n(Persistence)"
participant UserAgg as "User\n<<aggregateRoot>>"
participant JWT as "ITokenService\n(JWT)"

note over User, JWT
    Local login is shown (AA01). External login (AA02) ends in the same
    UserService.assertCanAccess() + issueAuthToken() and then in the same part 2.
    Wrong credentials keep the generic AA01 failure (401 "Invalid email or password").
    Every error branch ENDS the interaction: no token is issued or stored and /auth/me is never called.
    All errors use the errorHandler format { error: { message, status } }.
end note

== 1. Authentication (no role is accepted from the request) ==

User -> SPA : submits e-mail + password
activate SPA
SPA -> Routes : POST /api/v1/auth/login { email, password }
activate Routes
note right of Routes : rate limiter + Joi schema login\n(unknown fields such as "roles" -> 400)
Routes -> Controller : login(req, res)
activate Controller
Controller -> Service : login(LoginDTO)
activate Service
Service -> Repo : findByEmail(email)
activate Repo
Repo -> DB : SELECT ... FROM users WHERE email = $1
activate DB
DB --> Repo : row (roles, active) / no row
deactivate DB
Repo --> Service : user / null
deactivate Repo
Service -> Service : passwordHasher.compare(password,\nhash ?? dummyHash)

alt A) Unknown account or wrong password
    Service --> Controller : throw AppError("Invalid email or password", 401)
    Controller --> SPA : 401 Unauthorized\n{ error: { message: "Invalid email or password", status: 401 } }
    SPA -> User : show login error
    note right of SPA : interaction ends (AA01 generic message):\nno token stored, /auth/me not called

else B) Password verified
    Service -> Service : assertCanAccess(user)
    activate Service
    Service -> UserAgg : isActive()
    activate UserAgg
    UserAgg --> Service : active
    Service -> UserAgg : hasActiveRole()
    UserAgg --> Service : roles.length > 0
    deactivate UserAgg
    deactivate Service

    alt B1) Account inactive
        Service --> Controller : throw AppError("Account is not active", 403)
        Controller --> SPA : 403 Forbidden\n{ error: { message: "Account is not active", status: 403 } }
        SPA -> User : show AccessDeniedPage
        note right of SPA : interaction ends: no token stored, /auth/me not called;\naccount NOT reactivated (BR 5)

    else B2) Active account without any role
        Service --> Controller : throw AppError("No active role is assigned\nto this account", 403)
        Controller --> SPA : 403 Forbidden\n{ error: { message: "No active role is assigned to this account", status: 403 } }
        SPA -> User : show AccessDeniedPage
        note right of SPA : interaction ends: no token stored, /auth/me not called;\nCUSTOMER is NOT restored (BR 5)

    else B3) Active account with at least one role
        Service -> Service : issueAuthToken(user)
        Service -> JWT : generateToken({ sub, email, roles })
        activate JWT
        JWT --> Service : accessToken
        deactivate JWT
        note right of Service
            login() never calls save():
            roles and active state are unchanged.
        end note
        Service --> Controller : AuthTokenDTO
        deactivate Service
        Controller --> SPA : 200 OK { accessToken, tokenType: "Bearer", expiresIn, user }
        deactivate Controller
        deactivate Routes

        == 2. Only after B3: the SPA obtains the CURRENT internal roles from the back end ==

        SPA -> SPA : store token (AA04 mechanism)\nstatus = "loading" (no protected navigation yet)
        SPA -> Routes : GET /api/v1/auth/me\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>
        activate Routes
        Routes -> AuthMW : verifyToken(req, res, next)
        activate AuthMW
        AuthMW -> Service : resolveActor(token)
        activate Service
        note right of Service : token + account checks detailed in SD 3

        alt C) resolveActor fails (invalid token, user deleted, inactive, no role, roles not confirmable)
            Service --> AuthMW : throw AppError (401 / 403 / 500)
            AuthMW --> SPA : 401 / 403 / 500\n{ error: { message, status } }
            note right of SPA : handled in part 3 (fail closed)

        else D) Actor resolved
            Service --> AuthMW : AuthenticatedActor { sub, email, roles (from DB) }
            deactivate Service
            AuthMW -> AuthMW : req.user = actor
            AuthMW -> Controller : next()
            deactivate AuthMW
            activate Controller
            Controller -> Service : getCurrentUser(req.user)
            activate Service
            Service -> Repo : findById(UserId.create(req.user.sub))
            activate Repo
            Repo -> DB : SELECT ... FROM users WHERE id = $1
            activate DB
            DB --> Repo : row / no row
            deactivate DB
            Repo --> Service : user / null\n(invalid persisted roles -> AppError 500, D9)
            deactivate Repo
            note right of Service
                The account is re-validated on the instance
                that is returned: it may have been deleted,
                deactivated or left without roles after
                resolveActor() ran.
            end note

            alt D1) User no longer exists
                Service --> Controller : throw AppError("Invalid or expired token", 401)
                Controller --> SPA : 401 Unauthorized\n{ error: { message: "Invalid or expired token", status: 401 } }
            else D2) Found
                Service -> Service : assertCanAccess(user)
                alt D2a) Inactive
                    Service --> Controller : throw AppError("Account is not active", 403)
                    Controller --> SPA : 403 Forbidden\n{ error: { message: "Account is not active", status: 403 } }
                else D2b) No role
                    Service --> Controller : throw AppError("No active role is assigned\nto this account", 403)
                    Controller --> SPA : 403 Forbidden\n{ error: { message: "No active role is assigned to this account", status: 403 } }
                else D2c) Active with roles
                    Service --> Controller : UserResponseMapper.toDTO(user)
                    deactivate Service
                    Controller --> SPA : 200 OK { id, name, email, roles: ["CUSTOMER", "MANAGER"],\nactive: true, marketingConsent, createdAt }
                    deactivate Controller
                end
            end
        end
        deactivate Routes

        == 3. The SPA validates the answer before showing any protected functionality ==

        alt E1) 200 OK
            SPA -> SPA : user = authApi.parseCurrentUser(body)
            note right of SPA
                Valid only if: id is a "USR-" string, email and name are strings,
                roles is a non-empty array of DISTINCT values from
                {ADMINISTRATOR, MANAGER, EMPLOYEE, CUSTOMER}, active === true.
            end note
            alt E1a) Body valid
                SPA -> SPA : currentUser = user; status = "authenticated"\nnavigation built from user.roles (WEB03)
                note right of SPA
                    Roles are never decoded from the JWT and
                    never selected by the user. A user with several
                    roles sees the union of their sections.
                end note
            else E1b) Body malformed (missing / unknown / duplicated roles, active != true, ...)
                SPA -> SPA : currentUser = null; status = "guest";\ndiscard token (AA04)
                SPA -> User : "We could not confirm your permissions. Please sign in again."
                note right of SPA : protected functionality stays unavailable (fail closed)
            end
        else E2) 403 (account inactive / no role)
            SPA -> SPA : currentUser = null; status = "denied"; discard token
            SPA -> User : AccessDeniedPage with error.message
        else E3) 401 / 5xx / network error
            SPA -> SPA : currentUser = null; status = "guest"; discard token
            SPA -> User : "We could not confirm your permissions. Please sign in again."
            note right of SPA : only public (Guest) navigation (fail closed)
        end
    end
end

deactivate SPA

@enduml
